From 1c92af83e2c324f570c7d7a79d3741265667c160 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 23:42:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 103/106] slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: quitar el of_node_put de mas

El arreglo anterior soltaba a mano la referencia del of_node al dar de
baja el dispositivo, pero platform_device_release() YA la suelta:

  static void platform_device_release(struct device *dev)
  {
	  of_node_put(pa->pdev.dev.of_node);

Eran dos puts por cada get. Sobre un arranque limpio, 20 ciclos de
carga/descarga daban 16 avisos de refcount y kobject_del acababa sacando
el nodo hijo de sysfs para el resto del arranque ("Error -2 creating
of_node link" a partir de ahi).

El of_node_get() al asignar SI hace falta -el iterador _scoped suelta la
suya al salir del bucle-, y con el la cuenta queda: +1 del iterador / -1
del iterador, +1 nuestro / -1 de platform_device_release. Balanceada.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c | 21 +++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
index 78c5a1905..a3b3e9a58 100644
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -1713,18 +1713,17 @@ static int of_qcom_slim_ngd_register(struct device *parent,
 		/*
 		 * The device outlives this loop iteration, but the _scoped
 		 * iterator drops its reference on the way out - so take one of
-		 * our own, released when the device is unregistered. Without
-		 * it the node is only borrowed, and unregistering underflows
-		 * its refcount ("next of_node_put() on this node will result
-		 * in ... use-after-free").
+		 * our own. platform_device_release() is what puts it again.
+		 * Without this the node is only borrowed, and unregistering
+		 * the device underflows its refcount ("next of_node_put() on
+		 * this node will result in ... use-after-free").
 		 */
 		ngd->pdev->dev.of_node = of_node_get(node);
 		ctrl->ngd = ngd;
 
 		ret = platform_device_add(ngd->pdev);
 		if (ret) {
-			of_node_put(ngd->pdev->dev.of_node);
-			ngd->pdev->dev.of_node = NULL;
+			/* platform_device_release() puts dev.of_node for us. */
 			platform_device_put(ngd->pdev);
 			kfree(ngd);
 			/*
@@ -1918,15 +1917,13 @@ static void qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 * have worked, and took the phone down with it.
 	 */
 	if (ctrl->ngd) {
-		struct device_node *node = ctrl->ngd->pdev->dev.of_node;
-
 		/*
-		 * Read the node out first: unregistering may drop the last
-		 * reference to the device and free it. The reference being
-		 * released here is the one of_qcom_slim_ngd_register() took.
+		 * No of_node_put() here: platform_device_release() already
+		 * drops the reference that of_qcom_slim_ngd_register() took,
+		 * so releasing it again underflows the node's refcount and
+		 * kobject_del() takes it out of sysfs for the rest of the boot.
 		 */
 		platform_device_unregister(ctrl->ngd->pdev);
-		of_node_put(node);
 		kfree(ctrl->ngd);
 		ctrl->ngd = NULL;
 	}
